Carafe: the in-process server answers lock_file and unlock_file instead of "not implemented".
LockFileEx and UnlockFileEx failed with ERROR_INVALID_FUNCTION on every file, so a program that locks a file
before writing it gave up: FEX's disk cache created its file and never wrote it. The runtime is one process, so
no other process can hold a lock; the server grants every lock at once, the way Wine does on a file system without
locks, and the reply carries no wait handle.
LGPL-2.1-or-later, as the file it changes.

